- 1 => 1,000,000,000,000,000 - 1 = 999,999,999,999,999. So p_min = ceil((start - suffix)/B) = ceil(286,922,289,385,775 / 1e15) = 1? Actually start - suffix is less than B, so (start-suffix+ B -1)//B = (286,922,289,385,775 + 999,999,999,999,999) // 1e15 = (1,286,922,289,385,774) // 1e15 = 1 (since 1.286e15 // 1e15 = 1). So p_min = 1.\n\np_max = (finish - suffix)//B = (532,089,352,496,953 - 121,220,233,212,332) // 1e15 = 410,869,119,284,621 // 1e15 = 0? Actually 410,869,119,284,621 < 1e15, so floor division yields 0. So p_max = 0. Since p_max < p_min, answer = 0. So matches.\n\nThus DP would produce 0.\n\nNow test candidate(900407863935940, 961459078569857, 9, \"581747672523731\") == 0.\n\nCheck suffix digits: digits include 8,7,6 etc <=9. B=10^15? Actually length of s: \"581747672523731\" length 15. B=10^15. start-suffix? start = 900,407,863,935,940, suffix approx 581,747,672,523,731. start - suffix = 318,660,191,412,209, which is less than B, so p_min = 1? Let's compute p_min = (start - suffix + B - 1)//B = (318,660,191,412,209 + 999,999,999,999,999)//1e15 = 1,318,660,191,412,208 // 1e15 = 1. p_max = (finish - suffix)//B = (961,459,078,569,857 - 581,747,672,523,731) // 1e15 = 379,711,406,046,126 // 1e15 = 0. So p_max < p_min => 0.\n\nThus DP fine.\n\nNow check candidate(81, 861, 3, \"30\") == 3.\n\ns=\"30\", suffix=30, digits: 3,0 <=3 ok. B=100. p_min = max(0,(81-30+99)//100) = (150)//100 =1. p_max = (861-30)//100 = 831//100 = 8. p range [1,8]. Count numbers p in [1,8] with digits <=3: allowed p values: 1,2,3,4? Actually digit 4 >3, not allowed. So p: 1,2,3 only. Also p=0 not in range. So count=3. Good.\n\nNow test candidate(92, 914, 6, \"41\") == 6.\n\ns=\"41\", suffix=41, digits <=6. B=100. p_min = max(0,(92-41+99)//100) = (150)//100=1. p_max = (914-41)//100 = 873//100=8. p range [1,8]. Digits <=6: p values allowed: 1,2,3,4,5,6 (since 7 and 8 have digit >6). So count=6. Good.\n\nNow test candidate(9251, 82480, 9, \"49\") == 732.\n\nCompute suffix=49, digits <=9 ok