) if i % 2 == 0]\n    # forced start parity: 1 for odd, 0 for even, None if both possible\n    if O > E:\n        forced_start = 1\n    elif E > O:\n        forced_start = 0\n    else:\n        forced_start = None\n    result = []\n    start_parity = None\n    O_rem, E_rem = O, E\n    # position 1\n    if forced_start is not None:\n        # only one parity allowed\n        if forced_start == 1:\n            # odd start\n            cnt_per = fact[O_rem - 1] * fact[E_rem]  # O_rem > 0\n            idx = (k - 1) // cnt_per\n            x = odds[idx]\n            result.append(x)\n            odds.pop(idx)\n            O_rem -= 1\n            start_parity = 1\n            k -= idx * cnt_per\n        else:\n            # even start\n            cnt_per = fact[O_rem] * fact[E_rem - 1]  # E_rem > 0\n            idx = (k - 1) // cnt_per\n            x = evens[idx]\n            result.append(x)\n            evens.pop(idx)\n            E_rem -= 1\n            start_parity = 0\n            k -= idx * cnt_per\n    else:\n        # both parities possible\n        # each candidate (1..n) has the same block size\n        cnt_per = fact[O_rem - 1] * fact[E_rem]  # O_rem == E_rem\n        idx = (k - 1) // cnt_per\n        x = idx + 1  # numbers are 1..n\n        result.append(x)\n        if x % 2 == 1:\n            # odd\n            odds.remove(x)\n            O_rem -= 1\n            start_parity = 1\n        else:\n            evens.remove(x)\n            E_rem -= 1\n            start_parity = 0\n        k -= idx * cnt_per\n    # fill remaining positions\n    for pos in range(2, n+1):\n        required_parity = start_parity if (pos % 2 == 1) else (1 - start_parity)\n        if required_parity == 1:\n            # odd\n            cnt_per = fact[O_rem - 1] * fact[E_rem] if O_rem > 0 else 0\n            idx = (k - 1) // cnt_per\n            x = odds[idx]\n            result.append(x)\n            odds.pop(idx)\n            O_rem -= 1\n        else:\n            # even\n            cnt_per = fact[O_rem] * fact[E_rem - 1] if E_rem > 0 else 0\n            idx = (k - 1) // cnt_per\n            x = evens[idx]\n            result.append(x)\n            evens.pop(idx)\n            E_rem -= 1\n        k -= idx * cnt_per\n    return result\n```\n\nNow we need to verify that we correctly compute cnt_per for required parity each step, especially when O_rem or E_rem becomes zero. In those cases, cnt_per should be fact[0]*fact[remaining] = 1*fact[remaining] = fact[remaining]. But if required parity is odd and O_rem > 0, we compute cnt_per = fact[O_rem-1] * fact[E_rem]; If O_rem=1, O_rem-1=0 => fact[0]=1. Good. If O_rem=0 (should not happen when required parity odd), but we can guard.\n\nThus we need to ensure we don't compute cnt_per with O_rem-1 negative. But that case won't happen because if required parity odd, O_rem must be >0. Similarly for even.\n\nThus code safe.\n\nNow test for n=1: O=1,E=0,total=fact[1]*fact[0]=1*1=1,O==E? No, O>E, forced_start=1. cnt_per = fact[O_rem-1]*fact[E_rem] = fact[0]*fact[0]=1. idx = (k-1)//1 = 0. x = odds[0] = 1. Remove, O_rem=0. start_parity=1. k unchanged. Loop for pos from 2..1 none. Return [1].\n\nNow test for n=2: O=1,E=1,total=2*fact[1]*fact[1]=2*1*1=2, forced_start=None. cnt_per = fact[O_rem-1]*fact[E_rem] = fact[0]*fact[1]=1*1=1. idx = (k-1)//1.\n\n- For k=1: idx=0, x=1, start_parity=odd, remove odds[0], O_rem=0, E_rem=1, k unchanged. Loop pos=2: required_parity = start_parity if pos%2==1 else 1-start_parity => pos=2 even => required_parity=0 (even). cnt_per = fact[O_rem] * fact[E_rem-1] = fact[0] * fact[0] = 1. idx = (1-1)//1 = 0 => x = evens[0] = 2. Remove evens[0], E_rem=0. Return [1,2].\n\n- For k=2: idx = (2-1)//1 = 1 => x = idx+1 = 2. start_parity even. remove evens[0] (since evens list = [2,?] originally). O_rem=1,E_rem=0. k = 2 - 1*1 = 1. Loop pos=2 required parity odd: cnt_per = fact[O_rem-1]*fact[E_rem] = fact[0] * fact[0] = 1. idx = (1-1)//1 =0 => x=odds[0]=1. Return [2,1].\n\nWorks.\n\nNow test n=3: