500 is correct quotient. Remainder = 83,547,850.\n\nThus comb1 = answer1 * inv_S mod M = 83,547,850.\n\nNow we need to verify that this comb1 equals C(N-2, k-2). N-2 = 99998, k-2 = 65644. So we need to see if C(99998, 65644) mod M = 83,547,850. That's plausible? Let's try to compute approximate using some known combinatorial values? Hard.\n\nNow compute comb2 using expected answer 123,456,789.\n\nCompute comb2 = 123,456,789 * 923,552,229 mod M.\n\nCompute product: 123,456,789 * 923,552,229.\n\nWe'll compute similarly.\n\nLet a2 = 123,456,789, b = 923,552,229.\n\nBreak b into 923,000,000 + 552,229.\n\nCompute a2 * 923,000,000 = a2 * 923 * 1,000,000.\n\nFirst compute a2 * 923.\n\nCompute a2 * 900 = 123,456,789 * 9 * 100 = (1,111,111,101) * 100? Wait 123,456,789 * 9 = 1,111,111,101 (since 123,456,789 * 9 = 1,111,111,101). Multiply by 100 = 111,111,110,100.\n\nCompute a2 * 20 = 2,469,135,780 (since *2=246,913,578, times 10 = 2,469,135,780). Actually 123,456,789 * 2 = 246,913,578, then *10 => 2,469,135,780.\n\nCompute a2 * 3 = 370,370,367.\n\nSum: 111,111,110,100 + 2,469,135,780 = 113,580,245,880. + 370,370,367 = 113,950,616,247.\n\nThus a2 * 923 = 113,950,616,247.\n\nNow times 1,000,000 => 113,950,616,247,000,000.\n\nNow compute a2 * 552,229 = a2 * 552,000 + a2 * 229.\n\nFirst a2 * 552,000 = a2 * 552 * 1,000.\n\nCompute a2 * 552 = a2 * (500 + 50 + 2).\n\n- *500 = a2 *5 *100 = (123,456,789*5=617,283,945) *100 = 61,728,394,500.\n- *50 = a2*5*10 = 617,283,945 *10 = 6,172,839,450.\n- *2 = 246,913,578.\n\nSum: 61,728,394,500 + 6,172,839,450 = 67,901,233,950. + 246,913,578 = 68,148,147,528.\n\nNow times 1,000 => 68,148,147,528,000.\n\nNow a2 * 229 = a2*(200+20+9).\n\n- *200 = a2*2*100 = 246,913,578 *100 = 24,691,357,800.\n- *20 = a2*2*10 = 246,913,578 *10 = 2,469,135,780.\n- *9 = 1,111,111,101 (as earlier).\n\nSum: 24,691,357,800 + 2,469,135,780 = 27,160,493,580. + 1,111,111,101 = 28,271,604,681.\n\nNow a2*552,229 = 68,148,147,528,000 + 28,271,604,681 = 68,176,419,132,681.\n\