e also must handle modulo 1e9+7.\n\nComplexities: length up to 100, DP states: pos up to 100, prev digit 0-9 (including sentinel maybe -1), tight 2, started 2 => about 100*11*2*2 = 4400 states, fine.\n\nWe'll implement DP with memoization or iterative.\n\nImplementation details:\n\nDefine function count_leq(s: str) returns number of stepping numbers <= s.\n\nWe need to treat s as string of digits.\n\nPseudo:\n\n```\ndef count_leq(s):\n    n = len(s)\n    @lru_cache(None)\n    def dfs(pos, prev, tight, started):\n        if pos == n:\n            return 1 if started else 0  # if we have started, we have a valid number; else no number (exclude empty)\n        limit = int(s[pos]) if tight else 9\n        total = 0\n        if not started:\n            # option to not start yet: we can skip this digit (i.e., leading zero)\n            # But we cannot skip all digits; at end we need started True for counting.\n            # We can treat skipping as placing a leading zero, but we must ensure we don't count leading zeros as numbers.\n            # So we can call dfs(pos+1, prev, tight and (0 == limit), False)\n            # However, we must ensure that when we later start, the number doesn't have leading zero.\n            # So we allow \"skip\" (i.e., not started) and treat digit=0 as still not started.\n            total += dfs(pos+1, -1, tight and (0 == limit), False)\n            # start now with digit d from 1..limit (if limit >= 1)\n            for d in range(1, limit+1):\n                new_tight = tight and (d == limit)\n                total += dfs(pos+1, d, new_tight, True)\n        else:\n            # we have started, need to pick digit d such that abs(prev-d)==1\n            for d in range(0, limit+1):\n                if abs(prev - d) != 1:\n                    continue\n                new_tight = tight and (d == limit)\n                total += dfs(pos+1, d, new_tight, True)\n        return total % MOD\n    return dfs(0, -1, True, False)\n```\n\nBut we nee