_cost == INF: continue\n        # decode state to vector using division and mod.\n        # Compute new state id\n        new_id = 0\n        tmp = state\n        for i in range(k):\n            cur_val = tmp % base\n            inc = increments[i]\n            new_val = cur_val + inc\n            if new_val > p: new_val = p\n            new_id += new_val * powers[i]\n            tmp //= base\n        # Update newdp\n        new_cost = cur_cost + cost\n        if new_cost < newdp[new_id]:\n            newdp[new_id] = new_cost\n    dp = newdp\n\n- answer = dp[goal_state] if dp[goal_state]!= INF else -1.\n\nReturn answer.\n\nPotential bug: When we compute new_id we must consider contributions from dimensions beyond i (the higher dims). Since we compute new_id by summing new_val * powers[i], we need to also incorporate the unchanged values for dimensions beyond i? Actually we compute new_val for each dimension i and sum to new_id; that covers all dimensions. Good.\n\nBut we must ensure that we handle the case where plan increase is given as list length k. Yes.\n\nTesting: For state encoding/decoding we used loops; must ensure we use tmp = state initially, but after extracting each digit, we lose rest; we need to compute new_id using new_val for each dimension, but we also need to get the other dims' original values for dimensions where inc is zero? Actually we compute new_val = cur_val + inc. So we use inc each dimension. So we incorporate all dimensions.\n\nEdge Cases: The plan may have increments for each dimension up to p; fine.\n\nNow confirm DP works for k up to 5.\n\nPotential performance: copying dp list each iteration O(total_states) ~ 7776, times 100 = 777600, fine.\n\nPotential memory: dp list size ~7776, fine.\n\nEdge Cases: If n=0? Not given but could be. Then dp remains with dp[0]=0; answer is dp[goal] if goal=0 (i.e., p=0?), but p>=1, so answer -1.\n\nNow implement.\n\nWe also need to include typing imports.\n\nTest: Let's manually test with given cases a