sed as list of tuples; converting to tuple for dict key is fine, but we need to ensure the tuples inside are immutable. Yes they are ints, so fine.\n\nPotential nuance: In Python, default arguments are evaluated once. Use a global variable.\n\nNow implement:\n\n```\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\nclass DSU:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.parent = list(range(n))\n        self.rank = [0]*n\n    def find(self, x):\n        while self.parent[x] != x:\n            self.parent[x] = self.parent[self.parent[x]]\n            x = self.parent[x]\n        return x\n    def union(self, a,b):\n        ra = self.find(a)\n        rb = self.find(b)\n        if ra == rb:\n            return False\n        if self.rank[ra] < self.rank[rb]:\n            self.parent[ra] = rb\n        elif self.rank[ra] > self.rank[rb]:\n            self.parent[rb] = ra\n        else:\n            self.parent[rb] = ra\n            self.rank[ra] += 1\n        return True\n```\n\nNow compute:\n\n```\ndef compute_mst_mod_k(n,m,k,edges):\n    # edges list of (u,v,w) with 1-indexed vertices\n    # convert to zero-indexed\n    e = [(u-1, v-1, w) for u,v,w in edges]\n    best = None\n    target_size = n-1\n    # generate combos of indices\n    for combo in combinations(range(m), target_size):\n        dsu = DSU(n)\n        total = 0\n        valid = True\n        for idx in combo:\n            u,v,w = e[idx]\n            if not dsu.union(u,v):\n                valid = False\n                break\n            total += w\n        if not valid:\n            continue\n        # after processing n-1 edges, if no cycles, then connectivity is guaranteed\n        # because n vertices and n-1 edges and no cycles => it's a tree (connected)\n        # but we can double-check:\n        # root = dsu.find(0)\n        # if any dsu.find(i) != root: not connected => skip\n        # But it's guaranteed by tree property, but due to possible missing edges? Actually if graph is not