han 17.\n\nThus the best slash in range 1-66 might be earlier, perhaps with more twos after. For example slash at idx34: ones_before=9 (we computed), twos_after? Let's compute twos after idx34 within 1-66: twos at indices >34 up to 66: indices: 36 (2), 38 (2), 41 (2), 44 (2), 50 (2), 51 (2), 65 (2),66 (2). Also maybe at 30 (2) is before idx34. Also twos at 30 (2) is before slash at idx34? Actually idx30 is before slash at idx34, so not counted after. So total twos after idx34 up to 66 = 8. So min(ones_before=9, twos_after=8) = 8 => length = 17. Indeed slash at idx34 yields length 17. So answer 17 matches.\n\nThus algorithm yields answer 17.\n\nNow test candidate(s,20,70) expected 15. We'll trust algorithm.\n\nNow test candidate(s,73,76) expected 1.\n\nNow test candidate(s,53,73) expected 9. Let's compute slash at idx? We can trust algorithm.\n\nNow test candidate(s,30,31) expected 0. Substring \"2\",\"1\" no slash => 0.\n\nNow test candidate(s,47,63) expected 5. Substring indices 47-63: we previously computed answer 5. Good.\n\nNow test candidate(s,21,64) expected 9. We'll trust.\n\nNow edge cases: candidate('/',1,1) => 1.\n\nNow other tests: s = '/2//2/2/222//1//112//221/'.\n\nLet's parse this string and test cases.\n\nString: '/2//2/2/222//1//112//221/'. Let's index:\n\nIndices:\n1: '/'\n2: '2'\n3: '/'\n4: '/'\n5: '2'\n6: '/'\n7: '2'\n8: '/'\n9: '2'\n10: '2'\n11: '2'\n12: '/'\n13: '/'\n14: '1'\n15: '/'\n16: '/'\n17: '1'\n18: '1'\n19: '2'\n20: '/'\n21: '/'\n22: '2'\n23: '2'\n24: '1'\n25: '/'\n\nBut need to verify count: Let's write the string exactly: '/2//2/2/222//1//112//221/'.\n\nSegment by segment: \"/\" \"2\" \"//\" \"2\" \"/\" \"2\" \"/\" \"222\" \"//\" \"1\" \"//\" \"112\" \"//\" \"221\" \"/\". Let's expand.\n\nIndices:\n1 '/' (first slash)\n2 '2'\n3 '/' (first slash of double)\n4 '/' (second slash)\n5 '2'\n6 '/' (slash)\n7 '2'\n8 '/' (slash)\n9 '2'\n10 '2'\n11 '2'\n12 '/' (first slash of double)\n13 '/' (second slash)\n14 '1'\n15 '/' (first slash of double)