h at 15: sub[:15] = up to index14: includes everything except final slash. So ones_before = count '1's in indices 0-14: there are '1's at positions 4,7,8,14 => 4.\n\nNow compute suffix twos after each slash:\n\nWe need count of '2's after each slash.\n\nLet's compute total twos in sub: positions with '2': indices 0,1,9,12,13 maybe? Also maybe later? Let's list:\n\nIndex0 '2', index1 '2', index9 '2', index12 '2', index13 '2'. Also maybe index? No other '2's. So total twos = 5.\n\nNow for each slash compute twos after:\n\n- slash at 2: after index2 => sub[3:] = indices3-15: '/', '1', '/', '/', '1', '1', '2', '/', '/', '2', '2', '1', '/' => count '2's at indices 6? Actually we need to count positions: indices after slash at 2 are: index3 '/', index4 '1', index5 '/', index6 '/', index7 '1', index8 '1', index9 '2', index10 '/', index11 '/', index12 '2', index13 '2', index14 '1', index15 '/' => twos at index9,12,13 => 3 twos. So twos_after=3.\n\n- slash at 3: after index3 => sub[4:] = '1','/','/','1','1','2','/','/','2','2','1','/' => twos at positions: index? At sub index? Actually after index3, we have indices 4-15: '1' (no), '/', '/', '1','1','2','/','/','2','2','1','/'. Twos at index9? Let's count: sub index positions: after index3, relative indices 4..15: we have twos at relative indices 9 (original index9 of sub?), 12 and 13 (original index12,13). So twos count = 3 again.\n\n- slash at 5: after index5 => sub[6:] = indices6-15: '/', '1','1','2','/','/','2','2','1','/' => twos at positions relative 9? Actually within this sub segment, twos at sub indices 9 (original index9?), but we need to count. Let's list sub indices after slash at 5:\n\nsub[6] = '/' (index6)\nsub[7] = '1' (7)\nsub[8] = '1' (8)\nsub[9] = '2' (9)\nsub[10] = '/' (10)\nsub[11] = '/' (11)\nsub[12] = '2' (12)\nsub[13] = '2' (13)\nsub[14] = '1' (14)\nsub[15] = '/' (15)\n\nThus twos at indices 9,12,13 => 3 twos. So twos_after=3.\n\n- slash at 6: after index6 => sub[7:] = indices7-15: '1','1','2','/','/','