twos - prefix_twos_up_to_i.\n\nThus we need to compute prefix_twos cumulative count.\n\nLet's compute prefix_twos as we traverse from idx5 to idx76.\n\nInitialize twos = 0.\n\nIndices:\n\n5: '1' => twos stays 0.\n6: '/' => 0.\n7: '/' => 0.\n8: '/' => 0.\n9: '/' => 0.\n10: '/' => 0.\n11: '2' => twos becomes 1.\n12: '1' => 1.\n13: '1' => 1.\n14: '2' => 2.\n15: '/' => 2.\n16: '1' => 2.\n17: '/' => 2.\n18: '1' => 2.\n19: '/' => 2.\n20: '1' => 2.\n21: '2' => 3.\n22: '2' => 4.\n23: '2' => 5.\n24: '/' => 5.\n25: '2' => 6.\n26: '2' => 7.\n27: '2' => 8.\n28: '2' => 9.\n29: '/' => 9.\n30: '2' => 10.\n31: '1' => 10.\n32: '1' => 10.\n33: '1' => 10.\n34: '/' => 10.\n35: '1' => 10.\n36: '2' => 11.\n37: '1' => 11.\n38: '2' => 12.\n39: '1' => 12.\n40: '/' => 12.\n41: '2' => 13.\n42: '/' => 13.\n43: '/' => 13.\n44: '2' => 14.\n45: '/' => 14.\n46: '/' => 14.\n47: '1' => 14.\n48: '1' => 14.\n49: '/' => 14.\n50: '2' => 15.\n51: '2' => 16.\n52: '1' => 16.\n53: '/' => 16.\n54: '1' => 16.\n55: '1' => 16.\n56: '/' => 16.\n57: '/' => 16.\n58: '1' => 16.\n59: '/' => 16.\n60: '1' => 16.\n61: '/' => 16.\n62: '/' => 16.\n63: '/' => 16.\n64: '/' => 16.\n65: '2' => 17.\n66: '2' => 18.\n67: '2' => 19.\n68: '2' => 20.\n69: '2' => 21.\n70: '1' => 21.\n71: '2' => 22.\n72: '/' => 22.\n73: '2' => 23.\n74: '2' => 24.\n75: '/' => 24.\n76: '/' => 24.\n\nThus total_twos = 24 as we counted.\n\nNow for each slash at index i, compute suffix_twos after i = total_twos - prefix_twos_up_to_i (where prefix_twos_up_to_i includes any '2's at indices <= i). Since slash is not '2', prefix_twos_up_to_i = prefix_twos at previous index (i-1). But we can use the prefix_twos after processing i (which is same as before slash). Let's compute for each slash:\n\nList slash indices with prefix_ones (ones_before) and prefix_twos (twos_before). We'll compute twos_before = prefix_twos at index i-1 (the count of twos before slash). Then twos_after = total_twos - twos_before.\n\nBut careful: prefix_twos count at each index after processing char. We have values after each index (including that index). For slash at index i, we want number of twos after i, i.e., total_twos - twos_before (including any twos at i? but i is slash, not a 2). Since our prefix_twos array after processing index i includes any twos at index i (none). So we can use prefix_twos after processing i as twos_before. However, we need to know prefix_twos before slash (i.e., count of twos up to index i-1). Since slash at i does not affect count, prefix_twos after processing i is same as after i-1. So we can just use the prefix_twos value we recorded after index i (which is same as before). So we can use the twos count we tracked at each slash as the same as before.\n\nLet's compute for each slash:\n\nWe recorded prefix_ones for each slash earlier. Also we have prefix_twos count at each index (we have values after each index). Let's extract them for slash indices.\n\nWe'll create a table: slash idx, prefix_ones, prefix_twos (twos before slash), twos_after = total_twos - prefix_twos.\n\nNow compute prefix_twos for each slash.\n\nFrom above prefix_twos after each index:\n\nIndices with prefix_twos after processing:\n\n5: 0 (char 1)\n6: 0 (slash)\n7: 0\n8: 0\n9: 0\n10:0\n11:1 (after processing idx11 '2')\n12:1\n13:1\n14:2 (after idx14 '2')\n15:2\n16:2\n17:2\n18:2\n19:2\n20:2\n21:3\n22:4\n23:5\n24:5\n25:6\n26:7\n27:8\n28:9\n29:9\n30:10\n31:10\n32:10\n33:10\n34:10\n35:10\n36:11\n37:11\n38:12\n39:12\n40:12\n41:13\n42:13\n43:13\n44:14\n45:14\n46:14\n47:14\n48:14\n49:14\n50:15\n51:16\n52:16\n53:16\n54:16\n55:16\n56:16\n57:16\n58:16\n59:16\n60:16\n61:16\n62:16\n63:16\n64:16\n65:17\n66:18\n67:19\n68:20\n69:21\n70:21\n71:22\n72:22\n73:23\n74:24\n75:24\n76:24\n\nThus for slash at idx6: prefix_twos = after idx6 = 0. twos_after = 24-0=24.\n\nSlash idx7: prefix_twos after idx7 = 0 => twos_after=24.\n\nSlash idx8: same.\n\nSlash idx9: prefix_twos after idx9 = 0 => twos_after=24.\n\nSlash idx10: prefix_twos after idx10 = 0 => twos_after=24.\n\nSla