 23:'2'.\nSegment \"/\": index24:'/'.\nSegment \"2222\": indices 25:'2', 26:'2', 27:'2', 28:'2'.\nSegment \"/\": index29:'/'.\nSegment \"2111\": indices 30:'2',31:'1',32:'1',33:'1'.\nSegment \"/\": index34:'/'.\nSegment \"12121\": indices 35:'1',36:'2',37:'1',38:'2',39:'1'.\nSegment \"/\": index40:'/'.\nSegment \"2\": index41:'2'.\nSegment \"//\": indices 42:'/', 43:'/'.\nSegment \"2\": index44:'2'.\nSegment \"//\": indices 45:'/', 46:'/'.\nSegment \"11\": indices 47:'1',48:'1'.\nSegment \"/\": index49:'/'.\nSegment \"221\": indices 50:'2',51:'2',52:'1'.\nSegment \"/\": index53:'/'.\nSegment \"11\": indices 54:'1',55:'1'.\nSegment \"//\": indices 56:'/',57:'/'.\nSegment \"1\": index58:'1'.\nSegment \"/\": index59:'/'.\nSegment \"1\": index60:'1'.\nSegment \"////\": indices 61:'/',62:'/',63:'/',64:'/'.\nSegment \"2222212\": indices 65:'2',66:'2',67:'2',68:'2',69:'2',70:'1',71:'2'.\nSegment \"/\": index72:'/'.\nSegment \"22\": indices 73:'2',74:'2'.\nSegment \"//\": indices 75:'/',76:'/'.\n\nThus total length 76.\n\nNow we need substring from l=44 to r=56 inclusive: positions 44..56.\n\nPositions:\n44:'2'\n45:'/'\n46:'/'\n47:'1'\n48:'1'\n49:'/'\n50:'2'\n51:'2'\n52:'1'\n53:'/'\n54:'1'\n55:'1'\n56:'/'\n\nThus substring characters: at indices 44 to 56: \n44: '2'\n45: '/'\n46: '/'\n47: '1'\n48: '1'\n49: '/'\n50: '2'\n51: '2'\n52: '1'\n53: '/'\n54: '1'\n55: '1'\n56: '/'\n\nSo substring: \"2//11/22 1/11/\"? Actually string: \"2//11/22 1/11/\" but need to write precisely: \"2//11/22 1/11/\". Let's write sequentially:\n\n44 '2'\n45 '/'\n46 '/'\n47 '1'\n48 '1'\n49 '/'\n50 '2'\n51 '2'\n52 '1'\n53 '/'\n54 '1'\n55 '1'\n56 '/'\n\nThus \"2//11/22 1/11/\" but there's no space: \"2//11/22 1/11/\". Actually \"2//11/22 1/11/\". Let's just write as \"2//11/22 1/11/\". Wait we need to confirm characters at 50-52: 50:'2',51:'2',52:'1' -> \"221\"? Actually it's \"221\". Yes at 50-52 it's \"221\". So substring is:\n\n\"2//11/221/11/\"\n\nLet's write: index sequence:\n\n- 44: '2'\n- 45: '/'\n- 46: '/'\n- 47: '1'\n- 48: '1'\n- 49: '/'\n- 50: '2'\n- 51: '2'\n- 52: '1'\n- 53: '/'\n- 54: '1'\n- 55: '1'\n- 56: '/'\n\nThus \"2//11/221/11/\". Yes.\n\nNow compute answer for this substring.\n\nWe need to find slash with max k = min(#1 before slash, #2 after slash). Let's compute prefix ones and suffix twos.\n\nIndices in substring (0-indexed):\n0: '2'\n1: '/'\n2: '/'\n3: '1'\n4: '1'\n5: '/'\n6: '2'\n7: '2'\n8: '1'\n9: '/'\n10: '1'\n11: '1'\n12: '/'\n\nn=13.\n\nCompute prefix_ones array length 14.\n\nprefix[0] = 0\ni=0 char '2' => prefix[1]=0\ni=1 '/' => prefix[2]=0\ni=2 '/' => prefix[3]=0\ni=3 '1' => prefix[4]=1\ni=4 '1' => prefix[5]=2\ni=5 '/' => prefix[6]=2\ni=6 '2' => prefix[7]=2\ni=7 '2' => prefix[8]=2\ni=8 '1' => prefix[9]=3\ni=9 '/' => prefix[10]=3\ni=10 '1' => prefix[11]=4\ni=11 '1' => prefix[12]=5\ni=12 '/' => prefix[13]=5\n\nNow suffix_twos array length 14.\n\nsuffix[13]=0.\ni=12 '/' => suffix[12]=0\ni=11 '1' => suffix[11]=0\ni=10 '1' => suffix[10]=0\ni=9 '/' => suffix[9]=0\ni=8 '1' => suffix[8]=0\ni=7 '2' => suffix[7]=1\ni=6 '2' => suffix[6]=2\ni=5 '/' => suffix[5]=2\ni=4 '1' => suffix[4]=2\ni=3 '1' => suffix[3]=2\ni=2 '/' => suffix[2]=2\ni=1 '/' => suffix[1]=2\ni=0 '2' => suffix[0]=3\n\nNow evaluate each slash position:\n\nSlash at i=1: prefix_ones[1] = prefix before index1 = prefix[1] = 0 (since before slash at index1 we have char0 '2' which is not '1'). suffix_twos[2] = suffix[2] = 2 => k=0 => length=1.\n\nSlash at i=2: prefix_ones[2] = prefix[2] = 0 (since prefix[2] after char1 '/' still 0). suffix_twos[3] = suffix[3] = 2 => length=1.\n\nSlash at i=5: prefix_ones[5] = prefix[5] = 2 (since before slash at index5, we have two '1's at indices3 and4). suffix_twos[6] = suffix[6] = 2 => k = min(2,2) = 2 => length = 5.\n\nSlash at i=9: prefix_ones[9] = prefix[9] = 3 (ones at indices3,4,8). suffix_twos[10] = suffix[10] = 0 => k=0 => length=1.\n\nSlash at i=12: prefix_ones[12] = prefix[12] =5, suffix_twos[13] =0 => length=1.\n\nThus max length =5. So algor