 and insert all)\n    # but we can skip.\n\n    # bounded edit distance (Ukkonen)\n    INF = k + 1\n\n    # initialize previous row (i=0)\n    prev_low = 0\n    prev_high = min(m, k)\n    # dp[0][j] = j for j in [0, prev_high]\n    prev = list(range(prev_low, prev_high + 1))\n\n    # iterate i from 1..n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        low = max(0, i - k)\n        high = min(m, i + k)\n        cur_len = high - low + 1\n        cur = [INF] * cur_len\n        # iterate columns\n        for j in range(low, high + 1):\n            idx = j - low\n            # deletion (from s)\n            if prev_low <= j <= prev_high:\n                # prev[j - prev_low] is dp[i-1][j]\n                del_cost = prev[j - prev_low] + 1\n            else:\n                del_cost = INF\n            # insertion (into s)\n            if j - 1 >= low:\n                # cur[idx-1] is dp[i][j-1]\n                ins_cost = cur[idx - 1] + 1\n            else:\n                ins_cost = INF\n            # substitution / match\n            if j - 1 >= prev_low and j - 1 <= prev_high:\n                sub_cost = prev[(j - 1) - prev_low] + (s[i - 1] != t[j - 1])\n            else:\n                sub_cost = INF\n            cur[idx] = min(del_cost, ins_cost, sub_cost)\n        # early exit: if all values > k\n        if min(cur) > k:\n            return False\n        prev = cur\n        prev_low = low\n        prev_high = high\n\n    # after processing all characters of s, answer is dp[n][m] if within band\n    if prev_low <= m <= prev_high:\n        return prev[m - prev_low] <= k\n    else:\n        return False\n```\n\nWe need to ensure that we treat dp[i][0] correctly for j=0. In our loop we compute deletion cost for j=0, which uses prev[0] + 1 if prev covers j=0; for i>k, low > 0 so j=0 is out-of-band; but dp[i][0] = i (cost to delete i chars). However if low > 0, then dp[i][0] > k (since i > k). Indeed if i > k, then dp[i][0] = i > k, so we can treat it as INF (i.e., >k). So not