t-of-range (like del_off or ins_off), we set INF. For those we use INF directly, not INF+1.\n\nNow need to test the DP algorithm for some random strings to ensure no off-by-one errors.\n\nLet's test with Python mentally for simple case: s='a', t='a', k=0 (though k>=1 but test). n=m=1, diff=0 <=0. size = 1. prev for i=0: j up to min(m,k) =0 => prev[0] = 0 (since k=0). Loop i=1: j_start = max(0,1-0) =1? Actually i-k =1-0=1, j_start=1. j_end = min(m,i+k)=min(1,1)=1. So j range only j=1. offset = j - i + k = 1-1+0=0. sub = prev[0] =0; cost s[0]==t[0] => sub unchanged =0. del_off=1 > size => INF. ins_off=-1 <0 => INF. cur[0]=0. final offset = m-n+k =0. prev[0]=0 <=0 => True. Works.\n\nNow test s='a', t='b', k=0. size=1. prev[0]=0. i=1: j_start = max(0,1)=1, j_end=1. offset=0. sub=prev[0]=0 + cost=1 =>1. delete INF, insert INF. cur[0]=1. final dp=1 >0 => False. Good.\n\nNow test with k=1, s='ab', t='ac', distance=1 (replace b->c). n=2,m=2,diff=0 <=1. size=3. prev row: for j=0..1 (min(m,k)=1): prev[1]=0 (j=0 offset=1), prev[2]=1 (j=1 offset=2). Actually j=0 offset=1: prev[1]=0. j=1 offset=2: prev[2]=1.\n\ni=1: s[0]='a'. j_start=max(0,1-1)=0, j_end=min(2,1+1)=2. j=0: offset=j-i+k=0-1+1=0. sub = prev[0] INF, delete: del_off=1 => prev[1]=0+1=1, insert: ins_off=-1 INF => cur[0]=1 (delete 'a' maybe). j=1: offset=1-1+1=1. sub = prev[1]=0 + cost(s[0]=='a',t[0]=='a') cost=0 =>0. delete: del_off=2 => prev[2]=1+1=2. insert: ins_off=0 => cur[0]=1+1=2. cur[1]=min(0,2,2)=0. j=2: offset=2-1+1=2. sub = prev[2]=1 + cost(s[0]=='a',t[1]=='c') cost=1 =>2. delete: del_off=3 out INF. insert: ins_off=1 => cur[1]=0+1=1. cur[2]=min(2, INF,1)=1. prev=cur: [1,0,1].\n\ni=2: s[1]='b'. j_start=max(0,2-1)=1, j_end=min(2,2+1)=2. j=1: offset=1-2+1=0. sub = prev[0]=1 + cost(s[1]='b',t[0]='a') cost=1 =>2. delete: del_off=1 => prev[1]=0+1=1. insert: ins_off=-1 INF. cur[0]=min(2,1,INF)=1. j=2: offset=2-2+1=1. sub = prev[1]=0 + cost(s[1]='b',t[1]='c') cost=1 =>1. delete: del_off=2 => prev[2]=1+1=2. insert: in