anually using small script. But we can't run code here, but we can attempt to simulate with reasoning.\n\nBut we have enumerated pairs manually and got 10. DP should compute same.\n\nLet's simulate DP for [1,2,3,4] to be extra sure.\n\nWe will simulate DP step by step.\n\nInitialize dp0: dp[0][0]=1.\n\nProcess x=1:\n\ndp1 after first element:\n\n- from (0,0): none -> (0,0):1\n- assign to seq1 -> (1,0):1\n- assign to seq2 -> (0,1):1\n\nThus dp after first: dp[0][0]=1, dp[1][0]=1, dp[0][1]=1.\n\nNow process x=2:\n\nWe need to compute ndp from dp.\n\nInitialize ndp all zero.\n\nIterate over dp entries:\n\n(0,0) val=1:\n- none -> ndp[0][0] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=2 -> ndp[2][0] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=2 -> ndp[0][2] +=1\n\n(1,0) val=1:\n- none -> ndp[1][0] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=gcd(1,2)=1 -> ndp[1][0] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=2 (since g2=0) -> ndp[1][2] +=1\n\n(0,1) val=1:\n- none -> ndp[0][1] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=2 (g1=0) -> ndp[2][1] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=gcd(1,2)=1 -> ndp[0][1] +=1\n\nNow compute totals:\n\nndp[0][0] = 1\n\nndp[2][0] = 1\n\nndp[0][2] = 1\n\nndp[1][0] = from (1,0) none (1) + assign seq1 (1) = 2\n\nndp[1][2] = 1 (from (1,0) assign seq2)\n\nndp[0][1] = from (0,1) none (1) + assign seq2 (1) = 2\n\nndp[2][1] = 1 (from (0,1) assign seq1)\n\nAll other entries zero.\n\nThus dp after second element:\n\ndp[0][0]=1\ndp[2][0]=1\ndp[0][2]=1\ndp[1][0]=2\ndp[1][2]=1\ndp[0][1]=2\ndp[2][1]=1\n\nNow process x=3:\n\nWe'll need to compute ndp2.\n\nInitialize ndp2 all zero.\n\nIterate over each non-zero dp entry:\n\n1. (0,0) val=1:\n- none -> ndp2[0][0] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=3 -> ndp2[3][0] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ndp2[0][3] +=1\n\n2. (2,0) val=1:\n- none -> ndp2[2][0] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=gcd(2,3)=1 -> ndp2[1][0] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=3 -> ndp2[2][3] +=1\n\n3. (0,2) val=1:\n- none -> ndp2[0][2] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=3 -> ndp2[3][2] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=gcd(2,3)=1 -> ndp2[0][1] +=1\n\n4. (1,0) val=2:\n- none -> ndp2[1][0] +=2\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=gcd(1,3)=1 -> ndp2[1][0] +=2\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=3 -> ndp2[1][3] +=2\n\n5. (1,2) val=1:\n- none -> ndp2[1][2] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=gcd(1,3)=1 -> ndp2[1][2] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=gcd(2,3)=1 -> ndp2[1][1] +=1\n\n6. (0,1) val=2:\n- none -> ndp2[0][1] +=2\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=3 -> ndp2[3][1] +=2\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=gcd(1,3)=1 -> ndp2[0][1] +=2\n\n7. (2,1) val=1:\n- none -> ndp2[2][1] +=1\n- assign seq1 -> ng1=gcd(2,3)=1 -> ndp2[1][1] +=1\n- assign seq2 -> ng2=gcd(1,3)=1 -> ndp2[2][1] +=1\n\nNow sum contributions:\n\nInitialize all to zero. We'll sum each.\n\nFrom (0,0):\n- ndp2[0][0] = 1\n- ndp2[3][0] = 1\n- ndp2[0][3] = 1\n\nFrom (2,0):\n- ndp2[2][0] = 1\n- ndp2[1][0] = 1\n- ndp2[2][3] = 1\n\nFrom (0,2):\n- ndp2[0][2] = 1\n- ndp2[3][2] = 1\n- ndp2[0][1] = 1\n\nFrom (1,0) val=2:\n- ndp2[1][0] +=2 (now ndp2[1][0] = previous 1 +2 =3)\n- ndp2[1][0] +=2 (assign seq1) => ndp2[1][0] =5\n- ndp2[1][3] +=2\n\nThus after (1,0) contributions:\n- ndp2[1][0] =5\n- ndp2[1][3] =2\n\nFrom (1,2) val=1:\n- ndp2[1][2] +=1 (now ndp2[1][2]=1)\n- ndp2[1][2] +=1 (assign seq1) => ndp2[1][2]=2\n- ndp2[1][1] +=1\n\nThus ndp2[1][2]=2, ndp2[1][1]=1.\n\nFrom (0,1) val=2:\n- ndp2[0][1] +=2 (previous ndp2[0][1] from earlier was 1, now becomes 3)\n- ndp2[3][1] +=2\n- ndp2[0][1] +=2 (assign seq2) => ndp2[0][1] =5\n\nThus ndp2[0][1] =5, ndp2[3][1] =2.\n\nFrom (2,1) val=1:\n- ndp2[2][1] +=1 (previous ndp2[2][1] = 0? Actually we haven't added any yet. So ndp2[2][1] =1)\n- ndp2[1][1] +=1 (now ndp2[1][1]=2)\n- ndp2[2][1] +=1 (assign seq2) => ndp2[2][1]=2\n\nNow sum all entries:\n\nLet's list all non-zero entries after processing third element:\n\n- ndp2[0][0] =1\n- ndp2[3][0] =1\n- ndp2[0][3] =1\n- ndp2[2][0] =1\n- ndp2[1][0] =5\n- ndp2[2][3] =1\n- ndp2[0][2] =1\n- ndp2[3][2] =1\n- ndp2[0][1] =5\n- ndp2[1][3] =2\n- ndp2[1][2] =2\n- ndp2[1][1] =2\n- ndp2[3][1] =2\n- ndp2[2][1] =2\n\nNow process x=4 (value 4). That's last element.\n\nWe need to compute final dp after all 4 element