(g1,4))\n- Right: new_g2 = (g2==0?4:gcd(g2,4))\n\nWe'll compute contributions.\n\nWe'll need to sum all contributions.\n\nLet's denote each state (g1,g2) with count c.\n\nWe'll create a dict newdp.\n\nInitialize empty.\n\nWe'll process each state.\n\nI'll try to compute systematically.\n\nWe'll need to compute for each state:\n\n- Not use: add c to (g1,g2)\n- Left: add c to (new_g1,g2)\n- Right: add c to (g1,new_g2)\n\nNow we need to compute new_g1 and new_g2 based on g1,g2.\n\nWe'll go through each state.\n\nI'll create a table.\n\nState1: (0,0):c=1\n\n- Not use: (0,0)+1\n- Left: (4,0)+1 (since g1=0)\n- Right: (0,4)+1\n\nState2: (3,0):c=1\n\n- Not use: (3,0)+1\n- Left: new_g1 = gcd(3,4)=1 => (1,0)+1\n- Right: (3,4)+1\n\nState3: (0,3):c=1\n\n- Not use: (0,3)+1\n- Left: (4,3)+1 (since g1=0)\n- Right: new_g2 = gcd(3,4)=1 => (0,1)+1\n\nState4: (2,0):c=1\n\n- Not use: (2,0)+1\n- Left: new_g1 = gcd(2,4)=2 => (2,0)+1 (again)\n- Right: (2,4)+1\n\nState5: (1,0):c=5\n\n- Not use: (1,0)+5\n- Left: new_g1 = gcd(1,4)=1 => (1,0)+5\n- Right: (1,4)+5\n\nState6: (2,3):c=1\n\n- Not use: (2,3)+1\n- Left: new_g1 = gcd(2,4)=2 => (2,3)+1 (again)\n- Right: new_g2 = gcd(3,4)=1 => (2,1)+1\n\nState7: (0,2):c=1\n\n- Not use: (0,2)+1\n- Left: (4,2)+1\n- Right: new_g2 = gcd(2,4)=2 => (0,2)+1 (again)\n\nState8: (3,2):c=1\n\n- Not use: (3,2)+1\n- Left: new_g1 = gcd(3,4)=1 => (1,2)+1\n- Right: new_g2 = gcd(2,4)=2 => (3,2)+1 (again)\n\nState9: (0,1):c=5\n\n- Not use: (0,1)+5\n- Left: (4,1)+5\n- Right: new_g2 = gcd(1,4)=1 => (0,1)+5 (again)\n\nState10: (1,3):c=2\n\n- Not use: (1,3)+2\n- Left: new_g1 = gcd(1,4)=1 => (1,3)+2 (again)\n- Right: new_g2 = gcd(3,4)=1 => (1,1)+2\n\nState11: (1,2):c=2\n\n- Not use: (1,2)+2\n- Left: new_g1 = gcd(1,4)=1 => (1,2)+2 (again)\n- Right: new_g2 = gcd(2,4)=2 => (1,2)+2 (again) (since g2 becomes 2, which is same as original g2? Actually original g2=2, new_g2=2, same state, so (1,2)+2 again). So total addition for (1,2) from this state: not use + left + right = 2+2+2 